Add the novadeck stage-2 module.

One command, novadeck_bootattempts <image-name>, which opens
\SteamOS\conf\<image-name>.conf on the ESP of the disk this stage 2 was loaded
from, through the firmware's EFI_FILE_PROTOCOL, increments the boot-attempts:
value and writes it back.

This REPLACES Valve's steamenv, which did the same increment inside
steamenv_init and black-screened this device on 2026-08-02 without writing the
conf. See docs/phase5-bootattempts.md for the post-mortem; the short version is
that steamenv discovers the ESP by parsing SteamOS/partsets/* and matching
partition uuids across every SIMPLE_FILE_SYSTEM handle, and swallows the
failure when that lookup comes up empty. Here the image name is an argument
(gen-grub-cfg.sh already emits one config per slot and already knows the slot),
the conf is found by attempting the open on each handle in turn, and every
failure path returns a grub_error naming what was tried.

The handles tried are only those on OUR OWN disk, compared by the device-path
prefix that precedes the HD() node. Every novadeck medium carries the same
\SteamOS\conf\A.conf, so an unscoped sweep counts the boot on whichever volume
the firmware publishes first -- observed 2026-09-01 incrementing an internal
install's counter while a card was the medium actually booting. That count is
never cleared, because the Linux half (novadeck-bootctl mark-good) clears
through /esp, which is scoped to the booted disk. It climbs once per boot until
steamcl's failsafe rolls back a healthy slot.

GRUB cannot do this without a module: its own fat driver is read-only, so the
EFI file protocol is the only way to write the ESP from stage 2.

The file header carries the rest of the rationale, including why the ESP is
reachable from a binary chainloaded off the SLOT's efi partition, why the
loaded image can name our disk but not the volume we want, and why we
deliberately do not repeat stage 1's ConnectController sweep.

diff -urN a/grub-core/commands/efi/novadeck.c b/grub-core/commands/efi/novadeck.c
--- a/grub-core/commands/efi/novadeck.c
+++ b/grub-core/commands/efi/novadeck.c
@@ -0,0 +1,649 @@
